    <!-- project Doodad -->
    <div>
        <h1>Doodad Website</h1>
        <p>
            A website for SDEV 301 in the Green River Software Development BAS progam. Using Node.js,
            virtual machine servers, Express, dotenv, and SQL, I and two other classmates created a mock
            website to mimic functionality of modern websites. Our implementation ensured that we created
            secure webpages that prevent malicious attacks on our site and database, while maintaining a
            clean user experience on our site.<br>
            <a href="https://github.com/BROSKIs/doodad">Github link</a><br>
            <a href="http://137.184.36.197:3005/">Website link</a><br>
        </p>
        <img src="images/doodad.png" width="350" alt="A screenshot of the main page of Project Doodad.">
    </div>

    <!-- microjam -->
    <div>
        <h1>'26 Microjam</h1>
        <p>
            A microjam based off of the 2023 GBA Game Jam. Working with a partner, we created a small game
            using the Butano library inside a developer container, which we could import onto an SD card, then
            a game cartridge to be played on an actual Nintendo Game Boy!<br>
            <a href="https://github.com/DennysSaenz123/microjam">Github link</a>
        </p>
        <!-- Hi Tina! If you're looking at this, the game currently does not have graphics. -->
        <!-- It's not finished yet, so no screenshot as of now, but there will be one soon! -->
        <img src="" width="350" alt="A screenshot of the microjam in play.">
    </div>

    <!-- Amelia Bearheart -->
    <div>
        <h1>Bear Metal's "Amelia Bearheart"</h1>
        <p>
            The 2022 Season Competition Robot for the FIRST Robotics Competition team: Bear Metal 2046.
            Of the 4 years I spent on the team, "Ameila" was my favorite, as I personally programmed the
            visual targeting systems that the robot would use to shoot basketballs balls into a bucket.
            As a matter of fact, I originally gave inspiration to the name of the robot, "Bearheart", before
            it was officially named "Amelia Bearheart" by the team president at the time.<br>
            Unfortunately, the code for this robot is a secret, as it uses a team-specific library starting
            in year 2021. However, match information is available <a href="https://www.thebluealliance.com/team/2046/2022">here</a>
            with multiple videos of it in action!
        </p>
        <img src="images/amelia.jpeg" width="350" alt="Amelia Bearheart herself.">
    </div>

